Z||000000||gtsonly||05-31-2001||03:28 PM||||I am going to be doing a head job on my GT. Question is, would it be wise to go more of a progressive route on the valving or stick with a stock set-up for the valves? I have a stock 2.8  I have a set of heads striped down and ready to go to the shop or I also have a set from a friend that I may buy that already have been done to stock. he already paid for the heads and they are sitting in his garage. Next question, he said give him a price. I have a 2.8 block and crank and the undone set of heads, trade plus some cash. What is a good trade price?<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||6
